Given the function:
$$f(x)= \begin{cases} \sin{x}, & 0<x<1 \\ \cos{x}, & 1 \leq x \leq \sqrt{2} \\ \tan{x}, & x > \sqrt{2} \end{cases}$$
We observe that $1 < \frac{\pi}{3} < \sqrt{2}$, which falls in the second part of the function definition.

So, $f(\frac{\pi}{3}) = \cos(\frac{\pi}{3})$.

Now let's calculate the cosine of $\frac{\pi}{3}$:
\begin{align*}
\cos{\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} &= \frac{1}{2}
\end{align*}

Therefore, the value of $f(\frac{\pi}{3})$ is $\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}$.

