   &= \boxed{1}
   \end{align*}

2. First, let's simplify the given function:
   \begin{align*}
   f (α) &= \dfrac{2\sin (π+α)\cos (π-α)-\cos (π+α)}{1+\sin ^{2}α+\cos \left( \frac{3π}{2}+α \right)-\sin ^{2}\left( \frac{π}{2}+α \right)} \\
   &= \dfrac{\left(-2\sin α\right)\left(-\cos α\right)+\cos α}{1+\sin ^{2}α+\sin α-\cos^{2} α} \\
   &= \dfrac{2\sin α \cos α+\cos α}{2\sin^{2} α+\sin α} \\
   &= \dfrac{\cos α\left(1+2\sin α\right)}{\sin α\left(1+2\sin α\right)} \\
   &= \dfrac{1}{\tan α}
   \end{align*}
   Now, we find the value of $f\left( -\frac{23π}{6} \right)$:
